<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mpangazitha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1825">1825</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mpangazitha was a chief of the Hlubi, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguni">Nguni</a> people living near the upper Mzinyathi river in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwazulu-natal">KwaZulu-Natal</a>. Driven from their lands around 1818 by attacks during the upheavals known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mfecane">Mfecane</a>, he led a section of the Hlubi onto the highveld, where they raided and fought other groups. He was killed in 1825 in battle against the Ngwane of Matiwane.</p></div>
